			"Message": "fix(Sky): Convert workbench.js import to dynamic to avoid hard build failures\n\nChange Browser.astro to use dynamic import for @codeeditorland/output/vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench.js instead of static import. Static imports of unresolved package specifiers cause Rollup to hard-fail at build time, while dynamic imports only warn and allow the build to complete.\n\nAdd corresponding external resolution logic in astro.config.ts to pre-resolve @codeeditorland/output/vs/** package specifiers before Rollup attempts resolution.\n\nThis matches the import pattern already used in Mountain.astro, BrowserTest.astro, BrowserProxy/Workbench.ts, and Electron/Workbench.ts. Also apply minor formatting updates to Astro build artifacts in .astro/.",
			"SHA": "8a22169e2d6e984fd81a9d67846599216c2baf9d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T07:03:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				83,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Remove Wind package aliases from Astro Vite config\n\nRemove the explicit alias mappings for Wind packages from the Vite resolve configuration in astro.config.ts. These aliases were previously used to redirect @codeeditorland/wind/* imports to their static /Static/Wind/* paths, including Target prefix variants and Polyfills for the A3 Electron workbench.\n\nThis cleanup streamlines the build configuration. The alias resolution is now handled through other means or the imports have been updated to use direct paths.",
			"SHA": "b7f8d1b279aa25dd223d1794b65599c3ead4c56d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T06:32:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				83,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Normalize Astro build artifact formatting\n\nApply consistent formatting to Astro-generated type definition files in .astro/:\n- Update quote style from single to double quotes in content.d.ts\n- Add missing trailing newlines to collections.json and types.d.ts\n- Reformat multi-line type definitions for readability\n- Standardize reference path syntax in types.d.ts\n\nThese are build artifacts generated during the Astro build process. The changes ensure consistency with the project's formatting standards.",
			"SHA": "420f38ad95e6eaa65fe093809568bad5de8fae9b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T05:12:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				83,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Normalize Astro build artifact formatting\n\nApply consistent formatting to Astro-generated type definition files in .astro/:\n- Update quote style from double to single quotes in content.d.ts\n- Add missing trailing newlines to collections.json and types.d.ts\n- Reformat multi-line type definitions for readability\n- Standardize reference path syntax in types.d.ts\n\nThese are build artifacts generated during the Astro build process. The changes ensure consistency with the project's formatting standards applied in the previous commit.",
			"SHA": "e241025dba0cfdab91aabca689ba901f17d9e58c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:54:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				83,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Implement Tauri event bridge for sky:// channel communication\n\nAdd SkyBridge.ts - a new TypeScript module that subscribes to all `sky://` Tauri events emitted by Mountain and routes them to the VS Code workbench APIs or direct DOM manipulation.\n\nThe bridge implements handlers for 8 event categories:\n- Editor: openDocument, saveAll, applyEdits\n- Output: create/append/clear/show/dispose channels\n- StatusBar: create/update/dispose items\n- Progress: start/update/complete notifications\n- Terminal: show/hide/resize\n- Webview: message/dispose panels\n- Native: openExternal URL\n- UI: show-message-request, show-input-box-request, show-quick-pick-request\n\nMountain.astro now initializes the bridge after VS Code loads, exposing a `__CEL_WORKBENCH__` global proxy that provides access to VS Code's IWorkbench commands registry, environment APIs, and logger for SkyBridge to use.\n\nThis establishes the frontend half of the IPC channel between Mountain (Rust/Tauri) and Sky (TypeScript/Astro), enabling the backend to drive UI updates via Tauri events.",
			"SHA": "d33771494136ed7c2c3dc2aee7ffb99444594c7b"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778420684256
}